# Cursor Instructions — portfolio-hub

> Personal portfolio hub — luke-the-duke.com (Cosmic Intelligence).
> This file is a thin pointer. It holds no design rules of its own, so it cannot drift.

## Read before any UI or copy change

1. `BRAND.md`: the canonical design system (palette, typography, surfaces, motion and canvas layers, Do / Don't).
2. `DESIGN.md`: how design work is done in this repo.
3. `AGENTS.md`: commands, gates and repo conventions.
4. `src/app/design-system/tokens.css`: the token values. Never hard-code a colour; use the tokens.

If anything here disagrees with `BRAND.md`, `BRAND.md` wins.

## Hard rules (summary; details in BRAND.md)

- White on black, full contrast. No teal, green, blue or violet anywhere, in UI or scene code.
- Warm accents only, used sparingly: ember for alerts and classification, amber for signal heat, soft gold for rare highlights.
- The background is the single full-bleed black hole (one WebGL context, quality ladder, static still for reduced motion and no-WebGL). No starfield, grid or stardust layers.
- Text stays legible over the background; `node scripts/check-contrast.mjs` must pass.
- Canvas and WebGL never carry meaning; every visual has an accessible HTML equivalent.
- No invented numbers: every metric on the site comes from a recorded run with its source and date.
- Private projects show only what the catalog marks public; `npm run check:privacy` and `check:privacy:built` must pass.

## Exclusions

- **Bartlett Roofing projects** (BartlettBot, bartlett-permits) do not use Cosmic Intelligence branding. They have their own roof-industry theme; do not apply these tokens there.
